Market Challenges
Full-scale fire propagation testing requires specialised facilities, controlled test environments, trained personnel, and extensive safety procedures. Replicating realistic thermal-runaway conditions while protecting laboratory staff and equipment can be technically demanding.

Differences in battery chemistry, enclosure design, system configuration, and testing protocols also complicate standardisation. Providers must deliver reliable measurements and documentation that customers can use in their engineering and approval processes.

Market Restraints
High testing costs and laboratory lead times can limit adoption, particularly among smaller battery developers. Full-scale experiments may require substantial preparation, specialist resources, and dedicated testing capacity.

Limited availability of qualified personnel, restricted site access, integration delays, and pricing pressure can further affect project schedules. Some buyers may therefore choose phased testing programmes instead of commissioning extensive evaluations immediately.

